    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4172",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/24c2b0f28f2ae9eae92527191f0e97fb87aa1eb74323cf2d4b7f2f5fc2ecdd71.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of an even function?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the graph of an even function must be symmetric about the $y$-axis.\n\n- Graphs II, III, and IV are not symmetric about the $y$-axis. So, they are **not** even functions.\n\n- On the other hand, graph I is symmetric about the $y$-axis. That is to say, if we reflect graph I over the $y$-axis, we get the same picture. This means that graph I is an even function.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/b2598584b088e924dc518aa39d4adb1966f5670c827389c90bbf089dc50ee5e8.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
